setup-listener = Service listening ports
setup-listener-help = Both services bind only to 127.0.0.1. These ports do not change the current setup endpoint or automatically update the site origins above. Update reverse proxy upstreams or SSH tunnels accordingly. Checking does not probe port availability or binding permissions.
setup-public-listener-port = Public listening port
setup-public-listener-port-help = An integer from 1 to 65535, default 8090. Saved as 127.0.0.1:port; must differ from Admin. Ports below 1024 may require additional permissions.
setup-admin-listener-port = Admin listening port
setup-admin-listener-port-help = An integer from 1 to 65535, default 8091. Written to both Admin role and runtime configuration; must differ from Public. Ports below 1024 may require additional permissions.
setup-listener-conflict = Public and Admin listening ports must be different.
setup-advanced-reset = Restore advanced defaults
setup-advanced-reset-help = Restores only the log filter, Worker concurrency and polling, and realtime polling. Credentials, site origins, listening ports, and basic settings are unchanged. Check the settings again afterward.
setup-schedule-settings = Weekly auction schedule
setup-schedule-timezone = Schedule time zone
setup-schedule-timezone-help = Default UTC. Enter an IANA time zone, such as Asia/Shanghai, up to 128 UTF-8 bytes. Times below use this zone, not the browser's zone. The server checks time zone validity.
setup-schedule-preview-day = Preview weekday
setup-schedule-preview-day-help = Default Thursday. All stages must fall within the same Monday–Sunday week.
setup-schedule-preview-time = Preview time
setup-schedule-preview-time-help = Local HH:MM, default 22:00. Preview must precede opening by at least 120 minutes.
setup-schedule-open-day = Opening weekday
setup-schedule-open-day-help = Default Friday. Must not precede the preview weekday.
setup-schedule-open-time = Opening time
setup-schedule-open-time-help = Local HH:MM, default 00:00. At least 120 minutes after preview and before the nominal end.
setup-schedule-end-day = Nominal ending weekday
setup-schedule-end-day-help = Default Saturday. Must be in the same week as preview and opening; dates do not wrap to the next week.
setup-schedule-end-time = Nominal ending time
setup-schedule-end-time-help = Local HH:MM, default 12:00. Must be after opening; soft-close rules can still extend the actual end.
setup-day-monday = Monday
setup-day-tuesday = Tuesday
setup-day-wednesday = Wednesday
setup-day-thursday = Thursday
setup-day-friday = Friday
setup-day-saturday = Saturday
setup-day-sunday = Sunday
setup-schedule-order = In the same Monday–Sunday week, preview must be at least 120 minutes before opening, and opening must precede the nominal end. Cross-week schedules are not supported.
setup-title = First-run setup
setup-intro = Enter the one-time deployment code from the terminal. Use a local connection, SSH tunnel, or an explicitly authorized HTTPS proxy.
setup-confirm-initialize = I confirm this is a dedicated empty PostgreSQL database and authorize initialization and service startup after saving.
setup-initialize-help = Checking writes nothing. Confirming saves configuration, initializes the existing empty database, then starts Worker, Admin, and Public. Existing configuration is never overwritten.
setup-save-start = Confirm, save and start
setup-starting = Configuration saved. The server will initialize the database and start services. Check terminal readiness before opening Admin; on failure, inspect the saved configuration and database. Do not repeat setup.
setup-open-admin = Open Admin after the services are ready
setup-error-origin = Setup access was denied. Check the HTTPS origin, trusted proxy, or local tunnel.
setup-access = Step 1: Verify deployment code
setup-token = One-time deployment code (setup token from the terminal)
setup-verify = Verify and continue
setup-verifying = Verifying…
setup-verified = Step 2: Deployment code verified. Enter the database, administrator, and deployment settings.
setup-database = Database
setup-database-host = Database host
setup-database-port = Database port
setup-database-username = Database username
setup-database-password = Database password
setup-database-name = Database name
setup-database-help = Create the PostgreSQL 18 database and application role first. Enter the host, port, username, password, and database name separately; enter special characters as written. Validation checks connectivity; migrations run when the stack starts.
setup-admin = Administrator
setup-admin-actor = Admin username
setup-admin-secret = Admin password (at least 16 bytes)
setup-basic = Basic settings
setup-public-origin = Public site origin
setup-admin-origin = Admin site origin
setup-start-price = Default starting price
setup-metrics = Enable local metrics
setup-schedule = Enable automatic auction scheduling
setup-advanced = Advanced settings
setup-log-filter = Log filter
setup-worker-concurrency = Worker concurrency
setup-worker-poll = Worker poll interval (seconds)
setup-realtime-poll = Realtime poll interval (milliseconds)
setup-validate = Check connection and settings
setup-save = Save configuration and finish
setup-valid = The current input and database connection passed the checks. Nothing is saved yet; saving repeats the checks and validates the full generated configuration.
setup-complete = Configuration saved. Setup will stop; start the stack, then sign in to Admin for the remaining settings.
setup-error-input = Check the form values and try again.
setup-error-database = Cannot connect to PostgreSQL. Check the host, database, role, and password.
setup-error-config = The generated configuration did not pass validation. Review the settings.
setup-error-locked = Configuration already exists. First-run setup will not overwrite it.
setup-error-busy = Another setup request is in progress. Wait and retry.
setup-error-token = The one-time deployment code is invalid. Check the current setup server's terminal output and try again. Entered passwords have been cleared.
setup-error-io = Configuration could not be saved. Check directory permissions; services were not started.
setup-error-outcome-unknown = The save result is uncertain. Actions on this page are locked, and the deployment code and passwords have been cleared. Stop the setup process and inspect the target configuration directory first. Do not refresh to retry, delete files, or overwrite them.
setup-error-network = Cannot reach setup. Check the local connection or SSH tunnel.
setup-error-unknown = Unknown setup result. Check the server terminal before retrying.
setup-form-help = All input fields are required; advanced settings have defaults. Credentials stay only in this page's memory and must be entered again after a refresh.
setup-admin-confirmation = Confirm admin password
setup-database-host-help = Enter a hostname or IP, such as 127.0.0.1, without a scheme, port, or path. Maximum 253 UTF-8 bytes.
setup-database-port-help = An integer from 1 to 65535. The default PostgreSQL port is 5432.
setup-database-username-help = An existing PostgreSQL application account, up to 128 UTF-8 bytes. Enter it as written, without URL encoding.
setup-database-password-help = The database password, up to 4096 UTF-8 bytes. It must not be blank or contain control characters; enter special characters as written.
setup-database-name-help = An existing database name, up to 128 UTF-8 bytes, other than . or ... Setup does not create the database.
setup-admin-actor-help = Used to sign in to Admin. Maximum 128 UTF-8 bytes; no colons, line breaks, or null characters.
setup-admin-secret-help = Use 16–512 UTF-8 bytes without line breaks or null characters. Non-ASCII characters can use multiple bytes.
setup-admin-confirmation-help = Enter the same admin password again. This value is checked only in the browser and is not sent to the server.
setup-public-origin-help = For example, https://auction.example.com. Enter the exact origin without a trailing slash, path, or default port. HTTP is allowed only for localhost or 127.0.0.1.
setup-admin-origin-help = For example, https://admin.example.com. Follow the public origin rules and use a different origin.
setup-start-price-help = From 1000 to 1000000000, in multiples of 1000. Sets the default starting price for future auctions.
setup-metrics-help = Controls local metrics endpoints. Restrict access to trusted operators; do not expose them through the reverse proxy.
setup-schedule-help = Off by default. The schedule below is still saved and validated while off, without creating auctions. When enabled, Worker schedules future weekly auctions for main and isekai without changing existing auctions. Restoring advanced defaults does not change the schedule.
setup-log-filter-help = Default: info,auction=debug. Maximum 256 UTF-8 bytes. The server checks the full syntax; do not enter credentials.
setup-worker-concurrency-help = An integer from 1 to 8, default 4. Applies to this PostgreSQL deployment only.
setup-worker-poll-help = An integer from 11 to 300 seconds, default 15.
setup-realtime-poll-help = An integer from 100 to 5000 milliseconds, default 250. Controls Public server realtime event polling.
setup-advanced-show = Show advanced settings
setup-advanced-hide = Hide advanced settings
setup-advanced-help = Defaults usually suffice. Hidden settings are still submitted and expand automatically when invalid.
setup-save-help = Checking writes no files. Saving rechecks the database and generates configuration; it does not create a database, run migrations, start services, or overwrite an existing directory.
setup-validating = Checking connection and settings…
setup-saving = Saving configuration…
setup-errors-title = Correct these fields
setup-field-invalid = Check the format, range, and byte length against the guidance below.
setup-password-mismatch = The admin passwords do not match.
setup-origins-conflict = Public and Admin origins must be different.

